# MVNBC devices — EXAMPLE (dummy values for reference only)
# Format: vendor,ip,username,password[,enable_password[,ssh_port]]
# STANDALONE / LOCAL LAN mode: no Docker, no WireGuard, no portal needed.
# Just put the router's LAN IP here and run ./MVNBC.sh --auto from mvnbc/.
#   mikrotik,192.168.88.1,admin,CHANGEME
# Custom SSH port (inline or 6th field — both work):
#   mikrotik,192.168.88.1:2222,admin,CHANGEME
#   mikrotik,192.168.88.1,admin,CHANGEME,,2222
# Copy to devices.conf and fill in YOUR devices. NEVER commit real credentials.
mikrotik,192.0.2.1,admin,CHANGEME
h3c_1920,192.0.2.2,admin,CHANGEME
cisco,192.0.2.3,admin,CHANGEME
